### 3\. JavaScript / Node.js

Node.js provides command execution through its `child_process` module.

| Function       | Purpose                             |
| -------------- | ----------------------------------- |
| exec()         | Executes a command through a shell  |
| execSync()     | Synchronous shell command execution |
| spawn()        | Starts a process                    |
| spawnSync()    | Synchronous process execution       |
| execFile()     | Executes a program directly         |
| execFileSync() | Synchronous direct execution        |
| fork()         | Starts another Node.js process      |

Example:

```javascript
const { execFile } = require("child_process");

execFile("whoami", [], (error, stdout) => {
    console.log(stdout);
});
```

